[COMMENTS]
STATION,Long period of record from a rural catchment, includes daily flow record of a former, less accurate station Hatfield Peverel. GENERAL: Trapezoidal flume with throat tapping and low flow control, replaced less accurate station - Hatfield Peverel, 900m d/s, in 1964. Hatfield Peverel record held with this station (1932-1964). STATION HYDROMETRY: Theoretically rated. Modular limit ~0.2m, depending on downstream weed, no level yet recorded above 1.6m (structurefull). Scatter in gaugings beyond QMED caused by drowning. One peak flow rating applied across period of record. FLOW RECORD: No POT data are presented for this station as they have no non-modular flow correction applied. AMAX data have been corrected. Records in 1932-1964 are from a former, less accurate Hatfield Peverel station. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2020 (WINFAP Files v9). FLOW REGIME: Minor surface water abstractions for spray irrigation, small discharges from STW but net export through PWS.
CATCHMENT,London Clay, overlain with superficial deposits, mainly Boulder Clay and some sands and gravels. Rural, predominantly arable land.
Qmed Suitability,Gauged above QMED. Rating accounts for drowning.
Pooling Suitability,Many AMAX events are out of bank, and the rating makes no allowance for out of bank flow. Also, some spot gaugings show scatter from the rating.
[END]
